Lobium — native fingerprint config channel + first native surfaces (browser reads file → renderer reads base64).

The sidecar writes lobium-fp.json and launches Lobium with --lobium-fp-config=<path>. The renderer is
sandboxed and cannot read files, so — mirroring Chromium's own GaiaConfig file→switch serialization —
the BROWSER process reads the file ONCE (cached; base::ScopedAllowBlocking; kept off the per-spawn hot
path) and forwards its base64 to each renderer as --lobium-fp-data (with a Windows command-line size
guard). The RENDERER's lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current() (added module //components/lobium_fp, wired by
core/build-gn.patch) base64-decodes and parses it once and exposes typed fields; every failure path
LOG(ERROR)s (a present-but-unparseable config must never silently leak the host fingerprint).

Native surfaces hooked so far, each reading Current() (all PROVEN on Chromium 152.0.7928.0):
  1. navigator.hardwareConcurrency (navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc) — file value 7 vs host 12,
     consistent main-thread + Workers. --lobium-hwc=<n> retained as a single-value POC fallback.
  2. navigator.deviceMemory + the Device-Memory / Sec-CH-Device-Memory client-hint HTTP headers, hooked
     at their SINGLE shared source ApproximatedDeviceMemory::GetApproximatedDeviceMemory()
     (approximated_device_memory.cc) so the JS getter and the HTTP header report the IDENTICAL value
     (proven: config 16 → both JS and header report 16, not host 32). The configured value is snapped to
     a bucket this build actually emits (nearest power-of-two GB, clamped to desktop [2,32] / Android
     [1,8]) so it can never itself be an off-spec/out-of-range tell.
  3. navigator.maxTouchPoints (navigator_events.cc) — proven 0→5; overrides on the optional's
     has_value() so a desktop persona can force 0. NOTE: the paired touch surfaces (ontouchstart /
     TouchEvent / CSS pointer & hover media queries) are Settings-driven and NOT yet overridden, so this
     is coherent for a desktop persona (maxTouchPoints 0) on a non-touch host; full touch coherence for
     touch personas / touch-capable hosts is a follow-up (WebPreferences pointer_events_max_touch_points
     + available_pointer_types + the touch-event feature gate).

navigator.platform and navigator.languages are deliberately NOT hooked here — both are coupled to HTTP
headers (Sec-CH-UA-Platform / navigator.userAgentData.platform; Accept-Language) and must be landed in a
dedicated coherent UA-CH / locale patch, not as lone JS-getter overrides.

Four hook points:
  1. content/browser/.../render_process_host_impl.cc — browser reads --lobium-fp-config, forwards base64 --lobium-fp-data.
  2. third_party/blink/common/.../approximated_device_memory.cc — deviceMemory single source (JS getter + client-hint header).
  3. third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/navigator_events.cc — maxTouchPoints.
  4. third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc — hardwareConcurrency.

